; lang.xon -- what this bundle IS.

(lang "coreutils")

; HELIUM, plus exactly the libraries these applets import -- File,
; Sys, Proc, Date, Vector, Random, Hex -- and nothing ambient.  Radon is
; only a particular set of libraries to load, and the set it loads
; (the numeric tower, JIT-compiled tokenizer analysers) is the
; difference between a 12-second `ls` and a 3-second one; a tool that
; runs per file in a build cannot afford it (measured 2026-09-02).
; Self-contained like x-make: this bundle chains no dependencies.
; One bundle, many applets -- organized like busybox:
; `x -l coreutils -- sort -u file`.
(dialect he)

; v0.11.0: chmod, chown, ln, link, readlink, realpath, df, uname, arch, nproc,
; mkfifo, id, whoami, groups, logname, sync and nice all ride doors x-lang
; opened for this bundle (PR #607), and `install -m` applies the mode it once
; accepted and ignored. The bundle does not load without them.
;
; v0.14.0: (Err label e), which file-or-err (cu/prims.x) reads to tell an io
; error from any other raise.  v0.17.0 spells it
; (Err label e), and %cu-err-label takes whichever the platform has.
;
; v0.15.0: (Type named ...), which cu/prims.x fetches the string type's handle
; through.
;
; v0.19.0: (Http open), (Http read) and (Http close), the body a run at a
; time, which wget (cu/net.x) reads through -- and Tls connect, which
; raised after every handshake before it.
;
; Also (Sys catch-signal N) and (Sys take-signal N), (Term
; raw-with-signals! fd) and (Term measure fd), which vi's SIGWINCH, SIGTSTP
; and asking the terminal its size ride (x-lang#897).
;
; v0.23.0: (Socket send-to-run) and (Socket recv-from-run), binary UDP
; datagrams with their sender (x-lang#910), which tftp (cu/tftp.x) sends
; and reads its packets through, and the DNS server in the nslookup spec
; answers through.
;
; v0.24.0: a process record with its group, session, real ids and tty halves
; (x-lang#908), read in thousands of objects rather than hundreds of
; thousands (x-lang#912), which ps (cu/procps.x) reads for every process.
;
; v0.25.0: Lexer until rules that take their close or run to the end of the
; text (x-lang#920), which read vi's ex addresses (cu/vi-ex.x): a /pattern/
; whose closing / may be missing is one token.
;
; v0.26.0: the Lexer pattern rule, and a token that took the end text is cut
; back to the text (x-lang#929), which read printf, date and stat's format
; directives and echo's escapes (cu/fmt-lex.x): a trailing % is the directive
; % printf refuses by name.
;
; Also (Socket tcp-listen-on host port), a listener bound to one local address
; (x-lang#928), which httpd -p IP:PORT (cu/httpd.x) binds.
;
; Also (Host exe pid) and (Sys signals) (x-lang#926), which pidof matches
; an executable through and pkill names its signals through (cu/procps.x).
;
; v0.26.0 is the release the suite and its sweep bounds are measured on.
(requires-release "v0.26.0")

(entry "run.x")
